sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020, 2023) & Matsuda et al. (2020) human pluripotent stem-cell segmentation clock and metabolic tempo scaling model — MorphoEval overall 80.0/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 3 closes both v2 remediation items: Section 4b couples the delayed HES7 TTFL to DLL1-Notch delay signalling on a 12 x 12 hexagonal PSM lattice and reproduces the Matsuda (2020) Nature DAPT pulse-washout logic (slow partial synchronisation from random phases, R 0.19 -> 0.40; DAPT collapse; washout reset R ~ 1.00; Notch coupling retains R = 0.85 after 6 cycles vs 0.21 without coupling; collective period 298 min), with Herrgen (2010) coupling-delay and coupling-strength sweeps and an exact mean-field reduction proven in Lean; Section 4c adds a Matrigel elastic boundary force to a reduced 2D rosette model that epithelialises only when embedded (P_rad -0.08 -> 0.99 from 0 % to 10 % Matrigel, Spearman rho 0.94). The overall score nevertheless falls from 91.7 to 80.0 because the re-audit exposed that the 6-regime perturbation series is calibrated to the observed periods it is scored against (r = 0.9999 is circular), the 'human' cell is a rescaled mouse cell rather than the vendored Matsuda (2020) human kinetics, the kymograph is kinematic, the specimen is a chick SEM with a self-referential reference value, and two CLI parameters are dead. Those defects are now carried explicitly as Pass 4 remediation items. Overall 80.0/100 (faithfulness 76.4, reproducibility 88.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 72, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 74, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/human_somite_organoid_clock_comparison.png: rendered output of 2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py at d58a084, image/png, 1774211 B, 2775×2430 px, artifact_sha256 9f51f92b46d6a341eea40af3bf94cfb9d643809033460182d5d2873b9bd4c2d2 (sha256 9f51f92b46d6a341eea40af3bf94cfb9d643809033460182d5d2873b9bd4c2d2), spec_fingerprint dc5fc9fc0d0a3efa51f3e2df8dff0c42308ff7921502f484af6294b4b564fb24. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: dc5fc9fc0d0a3efa51f3e2df8dff0c42308ff7921502f484af6294b4b564fb24; artifact_sha256: 9f51f92b46d6a341eea40af3bf94cfb9d643809033460182d5d2873b9bd4c2d2; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/human_somite_organoid_clock/human_somite_organoid_clock_reference.json=b045a3f334ced9d4..., datasets/human_somite_organoid_clock/human_somite_organoid_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/human_somite_organoid_clock/scout_manifest.json=a3af01b1b2956954...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-human-somite-organoid-clock-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020) Nature 580:113-118: ~5.0 h (300 +/- 18 min) HES7-Achilles oscillations in human pluripotent stem-cell-derived presomitic mesoderm vs ~2.0 h (122 min) in mouse PSM | Matsuda et al. (2020) Science 369:1450-1455: species-specific HES7 intron splicing delay and protein/mRNA half-lives, not the hHES7 locus sequence, govern the ~2.5x human slowdown; intronless Hes7 abolishes oscillations | Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2023) Nature 613:550-557: mitochondrial ETC activity and cytosolic NAD+/NADH modulate translation rate and clock period (LbNOX acceleration ~228 min, azide/rotenone slowdown ~402 min) | Matsuda et al. (2020) Nature 580:124-129: a DAPT pulse followed by washout synchronises HES7 oscillations across hPSC-derived PSM cultures; Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007) Science: Notch inhibition desynchronises segmentation clock cells; Herrgen et al. (2010) Curr. Biol.: delayed intercellular coupling sets the collective period | Yamanaka et al. (2023) Nature 614:509-520 and Sanaki-Matsumiya et al. (2022) Nat. Commun. 13:2325: epithelial somite rosettes form only in Matrigel-embedded human axioloids / somitoids (qualitative); reconstructed_in_script: Delayed autoinhibitory HES7 TTFL RK2 DDE solver (mouse WT 122.00 min; rescaled 'human' cell 300.01 min), exact tempo-rescaling collapse across lambda in [1, 3] (max std 2.32e-13 nM), intronless-Hes7 subcritical collapse, and a 6-regime series whose per-regime tempo factors are hard-coded from the observed periods (Pearson r = 0.9999 is a calibration, not a prediction) | 6-species vertebrate clock allometry (r = 0.9970) from a vendored species table of delays/half-lives, a kinematic (not DDE-derived) axioloid phase-wave kymograph, and bilateral DoG somite segmentation on a chick embryo SEM (47.14 px mean spacing, CV 0.2010) | Pass 3: DLL1-Notch delay-coupled HES7 lattice (12 x 12 hex, eps = 0.25, tau_c = 0.8 T, 5 % tempo CV) through the DAPT pulse-washout protocol: R_0 = 0.19 -> R_pre = 0.40 after 5 coupled cycles; DAPT amplitude ratio 0.17; washout reset R = 0.9995; R retained after 6 cycles = 0.85 (coupled) vs 0.21 (coupling-ablated, lost at 3.0 cycles); T_coll = 298.2 min; in-phase stable for tau_c/T in [0.625, 0.95]; T_coll(tau_c) spans 235-417 min; R_end(eps) 0.26 -> 0.96 (eps 0 -> 0.25), 0.88 at 0.35 | Pass 3: reduced 2D cell-centre Matrigel rosette model: P_rad = -0.08 (0 %) -> 0.99 (10 %), epithelial fraction 0 -> 0.67, aggregate radius 85 -> 28 um, Matrigel sweep Spearman rho = 0.94; transfer_boundary: Single-cell / lattice HES7 DDE kinetics are compared with a chick (Gallus gallus) dorsal SEM, not with a human axioloid image; the 47.14 px 'reference' spacing is the script's own measurement recorded in the dataset JSON | tau_c = 0.8 T (240 min) is an assumption from delayed-coupling-theory stability, not a human measurement; the DAPT basal promoter fraction b = 0.1 and the competitive-promoter gate (synthesis and threshold both scaled by (1 - eps) + 2 eps S) are modelling reductions | Matrigel stiffness kappa = 0.01 min^-1 per % and the polarisation / constriction rate constants are phenomenological; the rosette reference values (P_rad = 1, contrast = 1) are geometric ideals, not measured organoid morphometrics; does_not_claim: Prediction of the LbNOX / azide / hHES7-swap periods from independently measured kinetics (they are encoded); 3D actomyosin apical-constriction FEM; Matrigel rheology; measured human Notch coupling delay; Floquet/stability analysis of the coupled DDE beyond the numerical lattice scan." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py:1034-1074 — kappa = 0.01 min^-1 per % Matrigel, phi_half = 4 %, and the rosette rate constants are phenomenological. Calibrate kappa to published Matrigel storage moduli versus concentration, extend the rosette to a multi-cell-layer ring with a lumen (or a 2D vertex model) and add a quantitative morphometric (rosette diameter, cell aspect ratio) comparable to axioloid somite sizes.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py:1733-1825 — the GIF still shows only the single-cell traces and the kinematic wavefront; add the lattice phase map through the DAPT protocol and the rosette relaxation so the animated artifact reflects the Pass 3 model, and vendor a requirements lock for this script.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py:402-416 — `evaluate_perturbation_series` overrides its generic lam_eff with observed-period constants (human WT = 300/122; LbNOX/azide = (300/122)*(0.41/k_met)) and the JSON k_met values (0.54, 0.31) are themselves 0.41*300/T_obs, so Pearson r = 0.9999 (measurement L1298-1307) is circular. Replace with a single predictive mapping from the vendored per-regime (tau_total, t_half_p, t_half_m, k_met) to DDE parameters (e.g. tau_i = tau_total * split, delta = ln2/t_half, alpha scaled by k_met) fitted on mouse WT only, report the out-of-sample RMSE for the other five regimes honestly, and drop the regime-specific branches.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py:549-599 — `simulate_axioloid_kymograph` is a prescribed cos(omega t - phase_lag(x)) wave with hand-set somite boundaries. Derive the kymograph from the Notch-coupled lattice (Section 4b) with an anteroposterior gradient of cell-autonomous period (or a moving determination front that freezes cells), so Panel D is model output and somite size S = v_wf * T is emergent.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py:608-623 and 1288-1297 — the 'human' cell is the mouse anchor dilated by 300/122 (tau_tx 30.5, tau_tl 13.1, t_1/2,p 38.1, t_1/2,m 35.9 min), not the vendored Matsuda (2020) human kinetics (tau = 51, t_1/2,p = 40, t_1/2,m = 42 min, JSON L123-140). Run the human regime and the Notch lattice from the measured human parameters (re-tuning alpha/K/n once), so that the 300 min period is a prediction rather than a construction, and wire `--tau-human` / `--thalf-human` (L1931-1932, currently dead) into that run.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py:836-837 and 143 — the Notch gate scales synthesis and repression threshold by the same factor and tau_c = 0.8 T is chosen from the stability scan. Derive the gate from an explicit competitive NICD/RBPJ vs HES7 promoter-occupancy model, and sweep tau_c jointly with eps to map the Arnold-tongue-like stability region (Panel H currently shows a single eps slice); report R_end(eps) beyond 0.25 where it becomes non-monotone (0.88 at 0.35).",
            "remediation needed: datasets/human_somite_organoid_clock/human_somite_organoid_clock_reference.json:56-90 and script 1318-1327 — the specimen is a chick embryo SEM and its reference spacing (47.14 px) is the script's own output. Vendor a CC-licensed human axioloid / somitoid image (e.g. from the Yamanaka 2023 or Sanaki-Matsumiya 2022 open supplementary data) or a digitised somite-size table from those papers, and compare the rosette model's aggregate radius (28 um at 10 %) and the lattice somite size against it." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
}

